From d8ccbd750900c88dc3bef1a94d672736ddb4ee35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris Brezillon <boris.brezillon@collabora.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 09:06:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] panfrost: Get rid of unused PAN_BO_ACCESS_xx flags

PAN_BO_ACCESS_{PRIVATE,SHARED} are neither set nor checked, so that one
is easy.

PAN_BO_ACCESS_{VERTEX_TILER,FRAGMENT} are set but never checked except
in panfrost_bo_wait() where we check if gpu_access is != 0, but because
those flags are never set without a R/W qualifier, the != 0 check still
works. Drop the flags along with the logic that was setting those flags,
and drop the stage parameter that was passed in multiple places to do
this selection.

Once this is done, we can move PAN_BO_ACCESS_{READ,WRITE} to bit 0 and 1.

Signed-off-by: Boris Brezillon <boris.brezillon@collabora.com>
Reviewed-by: Eric Guo <Eric.guo@nxp.com>
